Object.assign(ENEMIES,{
 warden:{name:"The Warden of the Cocoon House",hp:50,p2at:20,
  open:"He unfolds from beside the silk hammocks, a vast and tidy man with a darner's needle the length of a sword. \u201CGuests arrive by the front dock,\u201D he says, mildly. \u201CEverything else is inventory.\u201D",
  p2text:"The needle snaps. The Warden's tidiness goes with it \u2014 what's left moves like flood-water and grief.",
  moves:[{n:"Warden's Composure",kind:"stance",st:"iron",text:"He settles into stillness, qi lacquering over him in patient coats.",tele:"He is composing himself \u2014 lacquer-iron, layer on layer."},
   {n:"Silk-bind whip",d:6,drain:2},
   {n:"The furnace-line",kind:"heal",h:5,text:"A white line at his heel pulses, and the house's banked heat pours into him, knitting him whole.",tele:"The furnace-line glows at his heel \u2014 the house is about to feed him."},
   {n:"Threading the needle",kind:"charge",text:"He raises the darner's needle and the air threads itself through its eye.",tele:"The needle is threading \u2014 the Spindle Strike comes next."},
   {n:"Spindle Strike",d:12,kind:"release"}],
  p2:[{n:"Flood-water Form",kind:"stance",st:"flow",text:"He runs like water finding cracks \u2014 grief-fast, nothing held back.",tele:"His form is loosening \u2014 flood-water, no composure left."},
   {n:"Frenzied shears",d:8},
   {n:"Threading the needle",kind:"charge",text:"Half a needle still threads. His hands know the motion without it.",tele:"The Spindle Strike again \u2014 broken, hastier, still lethal."},
   {n:"Spindle Strike",d:11,drain:2,kind:"release"}]}});


SC["a3c19_plan"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER NINETEEN — THE COCOON HOUSE`)+P(`The riverhouse from Kang's last page turns out to be exactly what its paperwork isn't: beautiful. A long, low, lacquered building on black pilings out in the lake's quiet margin, white as the boat was, lanterns the color of weak tea — a place built to be mistaken for a rich man's retreat. The Court's counting room for eleven halls' tribute. And behind its water-gate, if the Frayed One's singsong schedule and Ruan's manifests agree — and they do — the room where the watershed's consignments wait for the Grand Loom.`)+((G.f.a3_furnace=="waiting")?(P(`You watched the inspection from a fish-boat two days ago: Madam Xian's white boat at Clearwater's dock at dawn, and at dusk a single closed palanquin carried aboard — the tenth bracket, the fattened beggar, half-fed and collected on schedule, exactly as your documents said it would be. You let it happen. You followed. Tonight the ledger of that choice comes due: he's HERE, behind the water-gate, and so is everything you waited for.`)):(""))+((G.f.a3_furnace=="freed")?(P(`Somewhere inside is one frightened abbot who rowed upriver with your description in his mouth — which means the house knows a weaver is coming. The lanterns are the color of weak tea, and there are twice as many lit as a retreat needs, and the quiet over the water has the specific texture of held breath.`)):(""))+P(`Your company, on the fish-boat in the dark: Ruan, checking the manifests one last time by hooded lamp, as if numbers might desert him at the hour they're needed.[[if G.sho>=3]] Granny Sho, at the bow, cane across her knees, listening to the house hum the way she listened to a mountain for forty years — “Two voices in that hum, boy. The little one is the beggar. Mind the big one.”[[end]][[if G.f.a3_mei_present]] And a sealed jar of Mei's best burn-salve in your bundle, delivered to the chandler's with a one-line note: <i>Whatever you're about to do, do it stitched. — M.</i>[[end]]`)+((G.f.a3_feral=="calmed")?(P(`And one more ally nobody can see: the Reed Wife's last gift, sung to you across the rice that final dawn — the water-gate's under-channel, the count of its chains, and the thing she remembered from inside: <i>the Warden drinks from a white line at his heel. Cut the line, and he is only a big sad man with a needle.</i>`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The water-gate, at the hour the lanterns gutter.`,go:"a3c19_house"}]};

SC["a3c19_house"]={img:"cocoon",
 t:()=>P(`Inside, past the chains and the counting room with its racked ledgers and its smell of mulberry and cold wax, the Cocoon House is the quietest room you have ever stood in, and the quiet is the obscenity.`)+P(`A nursery. That's what your eyes insist on: a long warm hall, lamplit the color of sleep, and down both walls, hung like cradles, hammocks of white silk — each one holding a sleeper wound to the chin in fine, fine thread, each thread running up through the rafters toward a banked heat overhead that sips, and sips, and sips. Seven sleepers. Seven souls in transit, fattened at seven kind franchises, waiting for the Loom. [[if G.f.a3_furnace=="waiting"]]The seventh hammock is newest: the beggar from Clearwater's gate, half-wound, breathing slow — the remainder you've been carrying since the ninth night, with a face.[[end]]`)+P(`You are three steps into the reading of the rafter-knots when the lamplight folds, and the Warden is simply THERE, between you and the hammocks, vast and tidy and sorrowful, a darner's needle the length of a sword held like a writing brush.`)+P(`“Forty years I have kept them warm and asleep through it,” he says, and his free hand straightens a silk cradle as he speaks, the gentleness of the gesture costing him nothing and changing nothing. “They never once hurt, weaver. Can the Loom say that of what YOU do to it?”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`It's going to hurt one of us. It always was.`,go:"a3c19_warden"}]};

SC.a3c19_warden={combat:"warden",win:"a3c19_freed",lose:"a3c19_cocooned",
 t:()=>P("The Warden bows \u2014 to the hammocks, not to you \u2014 and the needle comes around like a verdict.")+
 SYS("CLIMAX OF THE RIVERS AND LAKES. He composes in iron, floods into water, and the house itself reknits him by the white line at his heel \u2014 Snare the feeding, or cut him off it if you know how."),
 cstart:()=>{
  if(G.f.a3_feral==="calmed"){C.moves=C.moves.filter(m=>m.kind!=="heal");clog('<span class="good">The Reed Wife\u2019s gift, paid forward: your first knot was tied UNDER the floor an hour ago \u2014 the white line at his heel is already cut. The house cannot feed him.</span>');}
  if(G.f.a3_warned){C.charged=true;C.i=3;clog('<span class="foe">The abbot\u2019s warning bought him this: the needle was threaded before you crossed the water-gate.</span>');}
 }};


SC.a3c19_cocooned={img:"harvested",t:()=>'<div class="ending"><h3>ENDING: INVENTORY</h3>'+
 P("The silk takes you gently. That was always the house\u2019s one promise.")+
 P("They hang you among the sleepers, wound to the chin, and the banked heat overhead begins, politely, to sip. The Warden sits with you, as he sits with all of them, and his grief is real, and it changes nothing at all.")+
 P('<span class="small">But you are the only sleeper in forty years who can SEE the thread being wound \u2014 and a thread once grasped is never wholly lost\u2026</span>')+"</div>",
 c:()=>[{id:"r",l:"Grasp the thread. (Retry the Warden)",go:()=>{if(CKPT)G=JSON.parse(CKPT);else{G.hp=G.maxhp;G.thr=G.maxthr;}return "a3c19_warden";}},
  {id:"t",l:"Let it end. (Title screen)",go:"start"}]};


SC["a3c19_freed"]={t:()=>P(`The needle drops first. The Warden follows it down between the hammocks, lacquer and flood-water all run out of him, and the last thing his tidy hands do is straighten a silk cradle on the way to the floor.`)+P(`Then it's an hour of the truest work you've ever done: seven cocoons unwound thread by thread, your gold running along each fray like solder, seven sleepers lowered and warmed and breathing — and waking, one by one, into languages from four different skies. [[if G.f.a3_furnace=="waiting"]]The beggar from Clearwater's gate wakes last, half-spent, whole. You feed him Tang's last twice-baked cake and do not explain why your hands are shaking, and the ninth night's remainder finally pays out to zero.[[end]] Ruan moves down the counting room like a plague of one, cracking ledger-racks, and his laugh, when he finds the master tribute-rolls for the whole watershed, is not entirely sane.`)+P(`It is, for exactly that long, a complete victory.`)+P(`Then the lamplight folds again — and the house fills with mulberry.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Madam Xian is standing in the water-gate.`,go:"a3c19_marked"}]};

SC["a3c19_marked"]={t:()=>P(`She doesn't fight. She doesn't even frown. She stands in the water-gate in travel silk, taking a long, professional inventory of the wreckage — the freed sleepers, the dead Warden, the cracked racks — like an adjuster pricing a flood.`)+P(`“Seven consignments, one officer, one node,” she says at last, conversationally. “The costliest tantrum on this river in a century — and the Loom must still be fed, weaver, so the season-tithe will now be collected ELSEWHERE, in ways you have made less gentle. That arithmetic is yours to carry. We discussed how mercy is priced.” She turns to go, and pauses. The whole night has been waiting for that pause.`)+((G.sho>=3)?(P(`“The Court appreciates initiative,” she says, “and it does not punish candor. But it does take SURETIES.” Her sleeve moves once, the way a moth moves — and across the hall, a single white thread, fine as a hair, settles on Granny Sho's shoulder. It does not bind. It does not weigh. It lands like a name being written in a ledger, and it does not come off — your gold slides from it as if the claim were written on a page your patterns cannot touch. Sho goes still, then laughs, low and terrible. “Good,” the old woman says, to the silk on her shoulder. “Forty years I couldn't find the way in. Now the way in has claimed ME. Take me to my sister, you mulberry fool.”`)):(P(`“The Court appreciates initiative,” she says, “and it does not punish candor. But it does take SURETIES.” Her sleeve moves once, the way a moth moves — and across the hall, a single white thread, fine as a hair, settles on Ruan's shoulder. It does not bind. It does not weigh. It lands like a name being written in a ledger, and it does not come off — your gold slides from it as if the claim were written on a page your patterns cannot touch. Ruan looks at it for a long moment, then at you, and the measuring calm comes down over his face like the old iron veil. “Bookkeeping,” he says, quietly. “She has made me a line in your account, brother. Then let us go inspect the ledger.”`)))+P(`“Spring,” Madam Xian says, from the dock, not unkindly. “The Grand Loom, weaver. You were always going to come. Now you have a reason that isn't curiosity.” The white boat takes her, and the lake closes over her wake like a seam.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Dawn over the lake country, seven freed souls, and a white thread that doesn't come off.`,do:()=>{G.f.a3_marked=(G.sho>=3)?"sho":"ruan";},go:"a3c19_curtain"}]};

SC["a3c19_curtain"]={t:()=>P(`You sit on the riverhouse dock with the master tribute-rolls in your lap and the sun coming up over ten thousand boats, and you do the arithmetic — your kind, not theirs.`)+P(`Seven souls free. Eleven halls about to be audited by Yan's office, or Bao's whisper-network, or whatever the rolls make possible. One marsh quieter than it was. One bridge standing. One bride free. One sworn[[if !G.f.a3_ruan_sworn]] in everything but name[[end]] brother. And one white thread, on one beloved shoulder, payable at an address you finally hold: the Grand Loom, where a half-woven woman asks after the mountain, where the fraying of half a continent is held shut by stolen heat, where the Court of silkworms keeps its books.`)+P(`Mercy has a price tag. You've read it now, line by line. Spring is coming, and you are going to the Court — not as consignment, not quite as guest. As an auditor, with a debt to collect.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The river runs on.`,go:"end_book2"}]};

SC["end_book2"]={img:"title",
 t:()=>`<div class="ending"><h3>END OF BOOK TWO — THE RIVERS AND LAKES</h3>`+P(`The watershed is free of furnaces and the Court knows your name and your tea. A white thread rides a beloved shoulder toward spring. The Grand Loom is waiting — half a continent's fraying held shut by stolen heat, a sworn sister half-woven into its warp, and somewhere above it all, a Lady of the Reels who would so prefer you came willingly.`)+P(`${G.name}'s story concludes in <b>Acts IV–V: The Silkworm Court & The Pattern Sage</b> — the infiltration, Wen Suyin, the counter-pattern, and the door between worlds. The door below is open.`)+`<p class="small">Realm: <b>${REALMS[G.realm]}</b> · Insight ${G.insight} · Body ${G.body} / Mind ${G.mind} / Heart ${G.heart}</p>`+`</div>`+SYS(`Your journey is saved. The final book is here: the white city, the Grand Loom, and the end of the golden thread.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Continue to Act IV — The Frayed Heaven`,go:"a4c20_open"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Return to the title screen (your save is kept)`,go:"start"},
  {id:"c2",l:`⁂ Play again from the beginning (erases this save)`,do:()=>{localStorage.removeItem("gthread");G=fresh();},go:"start"}]};